Bugfix: Regenerate certificate bundles on upgrade

Outgoing HTTPS requests use a cached certificate bundle in the data
directory, which was only rebuilt when the bundled CA certificates had a
newer modification time. Deployments that preserve or normalise file
timestamps kept trusting root certificates that an update had removed. The
system certificate bundle and the user certificate bundles found in the data
directory are now regenerated during occ upgrade and occ maintenance:repair.

https://github.com/owncloud/core/pull/41910
